\title{Basic type constructors}
\import{prelude}

\p{As explained above, there are only really two things in the Coln language: types and elements of those types. We write \code{a : A} to express that \code{a} is an element of the type \code{A}. In this section, we describe informally the various type constructors available in Coln.}

\p{We now show how to build up progressively more complex theories via different type formers.}

\transclude{0031}
